|> Exercise
    handle=_double_post_processing_spteps_
    
    Let $f : \rr \ra \rr$, $A, B \in \rr$.
    Rewrite the two compositions below in the form
    $$
    x \ra \dots
    $$
    and describe how the graph of
    each composition relates to the graph of $f$.

    |> Image
        src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_POST_processing.svg

    |> Solution

        The first composition equals
        $$
        x \ra Bf(x) + A
        $$
        as illustrated here:

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_POST_processing_stops_1.svg
        
        Similarly, the second composition equals
        $$
        x \ra B(f(x) + A)
        $$
        (or
        $$
        x \ra Bf(x) + AB
        $$
        equivalently), as is easy to check. (No drawing!)

        For the second part of the question, since gluing
        the box

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Bz_alone.svg

        to the left of any function scales the graph of that
        function vertically by a factor $B$, while gluing the
        box

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Au_alone.svg

        to the left of any function translates the graph of
        that function up by $A$ (cf. Exercise 22), the graph 
        of the first composition...
        
        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_POST_processing_Bz_mid.svg
        ...is...
        
        __the graph of $f$ vertically scaled by $B$,
        |> br
        translated up by $A$__
            
        ...while the graph of the second composition...
            
        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_POST_processing_Au_mid.svg
        ...is...

        __the graph of $f$ translated up by $A$,
        |> br
        vertically scaled by $B$__

        ...as we reason by gluing the boxes onto the “$f$” box 
        one-by-one.